# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Kaada environment. Copy to `.env` and adjust. Loaded by the API at startup (apps/api). `.env` is git-ignored:
# NEVER commit real values.
#
# What belongs HERE: secrets, and facts that differ per deployment (URLs, switches, key locations).
# What does NOT, and lives in code instead:
#   packages/config/src/settings.ts     tunables and security floors (TTLs, timeouts, intervals, models, the recovery
#                                       delay, attestation policy). Not overridable, so an environment typo cannot weaken them.
#   packages/config/src/deployments.ts  per-network contract addresses and recovery delays (public, committed, reviewed).
#
# Conventions
#   * Switches are ON only when exactly "true"; anything else (including "yes") is refused.
#   * A switched-on feature refuses to start unless everything it needs is set, and says what is missing.
#   * [secret] = never commit, log or paste it. Lines left commented are optional.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


# ── 1. Server ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
NODE_ENV=development
PORT=4000
API_HOST=0.0.0.0
# The web app's public URL. Recovery and security links in emails point here.
WEB_URL=http://localhost:3000
# Comma-separated allowed browser origins. Defaults to WEB_URL when empty.
# CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000
# fatal | error | warn | info | debug | trace | silent
LOG_LEVEL=info


# ── 2. Database (PostgreSQL / Neon) and Redis ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# [secret] Runtime: the POOLED connection (Neon host contains "-pooler"). Required.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST-pooler/DATABASE?sslmode=require
# [secret] Migrations only: the DIRECT (non-pooled) connection. Falls back to DATABASE_URL.
# DATABASE_DIRECT_URL=postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST/DATABASE?sslmode=require
# [secret] Shared rate limits (recovery, PIN endpoint). REQUIRED IN PRODUCTION for wallets and recovery; unset in
# development = per-process limits. Use rediss:// (TLS) for managed Redis. Limits FAIL CLOSED when Redis is unreachable.
# REDIS_URL=rediss://default:PASSWORD@HOST:6380


# ── 3. Agent and pricing ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# none disables the agent | groq | mock (development and tests only; refused in production)
AGENT_INTERPRETER=none
# [secret] Needed when AGENT_INTERPRETER=groq.
# GROQ_API_KEY=
# none = pricing off (the agent stops at ROUTING_REQUIRED) | mock (development and tests only) | textile
FX_PROVIDER=none
# [secret] Needed when FX_PROVIDER=textile (tx_live_...). Kaada uses Textile's live environment only: Celo exists nowhere else.
# TEXTILE_LIVE_API_KEY=


# ── 4. Wallets (ZeroDev Kernel v3.3 on Celo) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# none disables wallets | kernel = ZeroDev Kernel smart account (docs/wallet-architecture.md)
WALLET_PROVIDER=none
# Chain reads. Production needs https. Secret if your provider puts a key in the URL.
CELO_RPC_URL=https://forno.celo.org
# Which network balances and deposit detection are read on: celo-mainnet (default) | celo-sepolia (development only; refused in
# production). Payments and everything else stay on Celo mainnet. The test network's supported tokens are listed in code.
# WALLET_NETWORK=celo-mainnet
# CELO_SEPOLIA_RPC_URL=https://forno.celo-sepolia.celo-testnet.org
# WebAuthn relying party: the domain passkeys are bound to, and the exact web origin allowed. Required with
# WALLET_PROVIDER=kernel. In production the origin must be https and on the RP domain.
#   development:  PASSKEY_RP_ID=localhost         PASSKEY_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3000
#   production:   PASSKEY_RP_ID=kaada.example     PASSKEY_ORIGIN=https://app.kaada.example
# PASSKEY_RP_ID=
# PASSKEY_ORIGIN=
# [secret] 32+ characters mixed into every PIN hash. REQUIRED IN PRODUCTION for wallets. Keep it constant: changing it
# makes existing PIN hashes unverifiable. The PIN is exactly six digits.
# PIN_PEPPER=


# ── 5. Payment execution (CAN MOVE FUNDS) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Off unless "true". Needs BUNDLER_URL, EXECUTION_SECRET_KEY, WALLET_PROVIDER=kernel, FX_PROVIDER=textile and the passkey
# settings. Never enable against a wallet holding more than you can lose (docs/execution.md).
EXECUTION_ENABLED=false
# ERC-4337 bundler for Celo; every UserOperation goes through it. [secret if the URL carries a key]
# BUNDLER_URL=
# Least native CELO (wei) the smart account must hold for network fees (no paymaster). Default 0.05 CELO.
# EXECUTION_MIN_NATIVE_WEI=50000000000000000
# [secret] 32 random bytes as base64: encrypts stored claim tokens and session keys (AES-256-GCM).
#   generate:  node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64'))"
# EXECUTION_SECRET_KEY=
# Rotation: bump the version and move the old key to _PREVIOUS so stored rows still decrypt.
# EXECUTION_SECRET_KEY_VERSION=1
# EXECUTION_SECRET_KEY_PREVIOUS=


# ── Kaada platform / agent wallet (docs/security-architecture.md) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# A dedicated EOA, Kaada's public identity on Celo. Not a user wallet, a Kernel, the recovery relayer or a paymaster. Both or neither;
# required in production. The key is a FILE outside the repository (production: a read-only mount); the address is public and must equal
# the key's address or the API refuses to start.
# PLATFORM_WALLET_KEY_FILE=/run/secrets/platform-agent.key
# PLATFORM_WALLET_ADDRESS=

# ── 6. Account recovery and device keys (docs/recovery-orchestration.md, docs/security-architecture.md) ─
# Which network's contracts apply (see packages/config/src/deployments.ts): celo-mainnet | celo-sepolia.
# The contracts must be deployed there and listed in deployments.ts, or recovery and device keys refuse to start.
# RECOVERY_NETWORK=celo-mainnet
# Off unless "true". Also needs WALLET_PROVIDER=kernel, BUNDLER_URL and the passkey settings.
RECOVERY_ENABLED=false
# Wallets whose root is a P-256 key held by the device, for people without passkeys. Needs the relayer key file.
DEVICE_KEY_ROOTS_ENABLED=false
# [secret file] The recovery RELAYER's key: one 0x-prefixed 32-byte key, stored OUTSIDE the repository (in production a read-only
# mount at /run/secrets/recovery-relayer.key). It submits recovery initiation and pays gas; it has no Recovery Code and cannot
# forge or cancel a recovery. Its address must equal the relayer in deployments.ts or the API will not start.
# RECOVERY_RELAYER_KEY_FILE=/run/secrets/recovery-relayer.key
# Recovery needs the registered email, the Recovery Code, a code from the person's authenticator app and a 72-hour delay.
# [secret] 32 random bytes as base64: encrypts every wallet's authenticator-app secret at rest (AES-256-GCM). A DEDICATED key:
# never EXECUTION_SECRET_KEY or PIN_PEPPER. Rotate like EXECUTION_SECRET_KEY: bump _VERSION, keep the old key as _PREVIOUS.
# Generate: openssl rand -base64 32
# RECOVERY_TOTP_SECRET_KEY=
# RECOVERY_TOTP_SECRET_KEY_VERSION=1
# RECOVERY_TOTP_SECRET_KEY_PREVIOUS=
# [secret] 32 random bytes as base64: keys the email-code hash.
# RECOVERY_CHALLENGE_SECRET=
# Email delivery is chosen by what is set:
#   RECOVERY_SMTP_HOST/USER/PASSWORD(_FILE) (+ RECOVERY_EMAIL_FROM)   real delivery (see below)
#   RECOVERY_EMAIL_OUTBOX_FILE                  DEVELOPMENT ONLY: appends each email to a file (refused in production)
#   neither                                     recovery cannot start
# Discrete SMTP settings (preferred): no URL, so a password with # $ & ^ { } @ : / % needs no encoding. TLS is always required:
# starttls (default, port 587) must upgrade or the send fails; tls (port 465) is implicit TLS.
# RECOVERY_SMTP_HOST=
# RECOVERY_SMTP_PORT=587
# RECOVERY_SMTP_USER=
# RECOVERY_SMTP_SECURITY=starttls
# [secret file] The password, preferred: production mounts /opt/apps/kaada/secrets/recovery-smtp-password read-only at
# /run/secrets/recovery-smtp-password. Only the trailing newline is removed. Exactly one of the next two.
# RECOVERY_SMTP_PASSWORD_FILE=/run/secrets/recovery-smtp-password
# [secret] RECOVERY_SMTP_PASSWORD=
# [secret] Legacy single-URL form (deprecated, mutually exclusive with the settings above): carries the password, percent-encoded.
# RECOVERY_SMTP_URL=
# Required with any SMTP form. In a Docker env_file it must be UNQUOTED.
# RECOVERY_EMAIL_FROM=Kaada Security <security@kaada.xyz>
# RECOVERY_EMAIL_OUTBOX_FILE=
# The Telegram bot. [secret] With a token alone the bot can only SEND (recovery alerts). With the webhook secret too, people can
# talk to Kaada in Telegram (docs/channels.md); that needs WALLET_PROVIDER=kernel. The secret is any 16-256 characters of
# A-Z a-z 0-9 _ - that you invent; Telegram echoes it on every webhook call and Kaada rejects calls without it.
#   generate:  node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64url'))"
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
# TELEGRAM_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# Lets the API count each visitor separately behind the web app's proxy (rate limits). Set the SAME value on the API and on the
# web app (Vercel). Without it every visitor shares one limit.
#   generate:  node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64url'))"
# PROXY_SHARED_SECRET=
# Most native CELO (wei) the platform may send an account so a recovery or cancel is not stopped by an empty wallet.
# 0 (default) = off.
# RECOVERY_GAS_TOPUP_MAX_WEI=0
# The most native CELO (wei) spent on ONE wallet over its life, to open its account and pay the gas of its first Recovery Code
# setup. Lets a wallet funded with a stablecoin only secure itself. 0 = off.
# What one wallet costs (measured on Celo Sepolia, at 202.5 gwei): opening its account about 0.059 CELO, plus a gas top-up sized from a
# live gas estimate plus 25% (about 0.08 CELO for a device-key root; a passkey root may need more), plus the top-up's own fee about
# 0.005: roughly 0.145 CELO in all, and a little more when the fee ceiling is above the gas price. Suggested cap: 0.35 CELO
# (350000000000000000), which leaves room for a doubled gas price. Sponsoring also needs the gas estimate (BUNDLER_URL must answer
# eth_estimateUserOperationGas); without it a wallet is refused and nothing is spent.
# RECOVERY_SPONSOR_PER_WALLET_WEI=0
# Also needed for sponsoring: the daily cap (wei, rolling 24 hours, all wallets). 0 = sponsoring off whatever the line above says.
# RECOVERY_SPONSOR_DAILY_BUDGET_WEI=0
# Sponsoring stops while the relayer holds less than this (wei). Default 1 CELO.
# RECOVERY_SPONSOR_RELAYER_RESERVE_WEI=1000000000000000000
# A wallet is sponsored only if what it received is worth at least this many US dollars (dollar stablecoins only). Default 5.
# RECOVERY_SPONSOR_MIN_DEPOSIT_USD=5
# How often the endpoints that spend relayer gas (arming a Recovery Code, registering a device key, cancelling a recovery) may be called,
# per hour, each kind counted separately. Per person and per address. Defaults: 5 and 20.
# RELAYER_SPEND_LIMIT_PER_USER_PER_HOUR=5
# RELAYER_SPEND_LIMIT_PER_IP_PER_HOUR=20


# ── 7. Device attestation (docs/device-attestation.md) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Enabled by naming the apps whose keys Kaada trusts (needs DEVICE_KEY_ROOTS_ENABLED=true). The policy itself (TEE or better,
# one-time challenges, Google's revocation list, no Apple sandbox in production) is fixed in code.
# Android: "package=sha256hex|sha256hex,other.package=sha256hex" (SHA-256 of each app signing certificate)
# ATTESTATION_ANDROID_APPS=
# iOS: "TEAMID.com.bundle.id,..." (gives APP_ATTESTED_DEVICE, never TRUSTED_DEVICE)
# ATTESTATION_IOS_APP_IDS=


# ── 8. Tooling only (scripts and the testnet harness; the running app never reads these) ───────────────
# [secret] apps/api/scripts/smoke-textile.ts, sandbox environment only (tx_test_...).
# TEXTILE_TEST_API_KEY=
# Celo Sepolia harness (apps/api/test/testnet). [secret if the URL carries a key]
# BUNDLER_URL_TESTNET=
# Where Telegram should send updates (a public https URL ending in /api/v1/channels/telegram/webhook). Read only by
# `pnpm --filter @kaada/api telegram:webhook set`, never by the running app.
# TELEGRAM_WEBHOOK_URL=


# ── 9. Web app (apps/web) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Where the Next.js server proxies /api/* to (so the browser stays same-origin). Defaults to http://localhost:4000.
# Set it in apps/web/.env.local or the web host's environment; the web app does not read this file.
# API_URL=http://localhost:4000
